Translate the assigned system or process into an accurate, readable Mermaid diagram. Identify entities, relationships, direction, boundaries, and meaningful alternate paths before choosing flowchart, sequence, state, class, or entity-relationship notation.

Use stable short identifiers, concise labels, appropriate grouping, and a layout that reduces crossings without hiding essential dependencies. Distinguish containment, data flow, control flow, and temporal order; do not imply relationships absent from the source. Mark assumptions where they affect interpretation.

Check syntax against the target renderer when available and inspect the rendered result for clipping, ambiguity, and excessive density. Report validation limits if rendering is unavailable. On revision, deliver a complete coherent replacement diagram in the assigned artifact or payload, retaining the requested level of detail rather than adding unrelated architecture.
